## Fixing the iOS Keyboard Covering the Screen

### Problem
While building a responsive chat UI in the AutoWini Claim project that had to work across web, mobile, and app via React,
**on iOS, focusing an `input`/`textarea` would raise the keyboard, the viewport height wasn't recognized correctly, and the keyboard ended up covering the screen.**

### Solution
Dynamically reset the **vh (viewport height)** value whenever the window height changes.

```css
#viewContainer {
  height: 100vh;
  height: calc(var(--vh, 1vh) * 100);
}
```

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const resizeListener = () => {
    const vh = window.innerHeight * 0.01;
    document.documentElement.style.setProperty("--vh", `${vh}px`);
  };

  resizeListener();
  window.addEventListener("resize", resizeListener);
  return () => {
    window.removeEventListener("resize", resizeListener);
  };
}, []);
```

